 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, you can go jogging in Penang. The air quality is **Moderate** across the state, with AQI readings ranging between **55 and 82** (depending on the specific area, such as Balik Pulau, George Town, Minden, or Perai). \n\n### What to Expect:\n* **Air Quality:** An AQI in the 51–100 (Moderate) range is completely acceptable for outdoor exercise for the general public. However, if you have asthma or are unusually sensitive to air pollution (primarily PM2.5), you may want to keep your jog light or shorten the duration.\n* **Weather & Timing:** Note that it is past midnight in Penang (12:45 AM MYT). Temperatures are hovering around 27°C–28°C (81°F–83°F) with high humidity, and there is a chance of scattered thunderstorms moving through overnight into Sunday. \n\nIf you are heading out for a late-night or early-morning run, the air is safe enough to do so—just keep an eye on the radar for rain and stick to well-lit routes!",
